<title>USA: Telesystem Int'l sells $200 mln 144A notes.</title>
<headline>Telesystem Int'l sells $200 mln 144A notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following 144a debt issue from Telesystem International Wireless Inc was priced on Tuesday via co-lead managers Goldman Sachs &amp; Co and CIBC Wood Gundy Securities Corp, according to market sources.</p>
<p>BORROWER TELESYSTEM INTERNATIONAL WIRELESS INC</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	  COUPON 5-YR ZERO MATURITY 6/30/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SNR DISC NOTES ISS PRICE 52.595 FIRST PAY DATE 12/30/1997 LAST MOODY'S CAA1   YTM 13.25 PCT    PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-MINUS    SPREAD 683 BP    CALLABLE  NON-CALL FIVE</p>
<p>NOTES: The notes are $200 million of proceeds and have a three-year equity call for 35 percent at 113.25.</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678 ))</p>
</text>
